  "name": "atx-v1_1/integer-outside-exact-range",
  "description": "An ATX v1.1 credential carrying scanSummary.criticalFindings 9007199254740993, which is 2^53+1 and outside the I-JSON exact range, -(2^53-1) to 2^53-1 (RFC 7493 §2.2). Its Ed25519 signature covers JCS(TBS) as an RFC 8785 serializer that reads each number as an IEEE 754 double writes it, with criticalFindings 9007199254740992: the bytes that serializer writes for a credential carrying 9007199254740992 too. The signature does not tell the two counts apart, so it does not cover the count this credential carries (atx-spec §1.3a.2 rule 3 keeps RFC 8785 number serialization out of cross-language scope). The verifier MUST REJECT with a signature-validation reason. A verifier that canonicalizes the count as that serializer does verifies the signature and wrongly ACCEPTs a count its signature does not cover.",
  "requirement": "§1.3a.2 rule 3: RFC 8785 number serialization is kept out of cross-language scope, and outside the I-JSON exact range it does not write every integer as its digits, so criticalFindings 9007199254740993, which it writes as 9007199254740992, has no value the signature covers and is a signature failure",
